{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Capability-link semantics (docs/page-links.md §1, §4-§6), for the app that serves links. `delegation`: a creator's current authority and a requested link, with the mint result. `use_sequence`: one link's ordered steps (b-17/b-18 bookings; projection {arrival, status}; mark-cleaned constrained to b-17), each with its expected result; same_receipt_as names a step index (0-based). `race`: orderings of concurrent transactions under the link's row lock. `lockout`: exchange rate limiting that a stranger knowing a link_id cannot use against its holder. `replay_cases` separate operation retries (fresh nonce, same idempotency key: the stored receipt, after use or revocation, while the session is live) from nonce replays (refused, even after a refused action). `asset_sequence` and `grant_expiry` cover asset grants for native image and video loads. Unless a step says otherwise, writes carry the right Origin and the session's CSRF token.",
  "delegation": [
    {
      "name": "within-creator-authority",
      "creator": {
        "reads": {
          "bookings": {
            "records": [
              "b-17",
              "b-18"
            ],
            "fields": [
              "arrival",
              "departure",
              "status",
              "guest_note"
            ]
          }
        },
        "actions": [
          "mark-cleaned",
          "request-cleaner"
        ]
      },
      "link": {
        "projection": {
          "bookings": {
            "records": [
              "b-17"
            ],
            "fields": [
              "arrival",
              "status"
            ]
          }
        },
        "actions": [
          {
            "action_id": "mark-cleaned",
            "constraints": {
              "record_id": "b-17"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "minted": true
      }
    },
    {
